WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.612
Beyond the hosts, a script still
has two things to get right.

2
00:00:03.612 --> 00:00:06.062
The token's scope names the resource.

3
00:00:06.062 --> 00:00:11.548
App-only tokens for Graph in worldwide and
GCC tenants ask for graph dot microsoft

4
00:00:11.548 --> 00:00:16.712
dot com slash dot default, the form
Microsoft's client-credentials guide uses.

5
00:00:16.712 --> 00:00:20.037
And each API page lists
the clouds it works in.

6
00:00:20.037 --> 00:00:25.488
Every Graph API reference page has a
national cloud table, and most of the

7
00:00:25.488 --> 00:00:30.938
Entra APIs in Module 2 are available
in the global service, which GCC uses.

8
00:00:30.938 --> 00:00:33.903
Check the table before you rely on an API.

9
00:00:33.903 --> 00:00:36.418
GCC uses the worldwide endpoints,

10
00:00:36.418 --> 00:00:41.988
but some features available in commercial
tenants aren't available in GCC.

11
00:00:41.988 --> 00:00:44.887
That's a feature question,
not an endpoint question.

12
00:00:44.887 --> 00:00:49.956
The Federal Modernization Workbook's Cloud
Boundary and Landing Zone book covers it,

13
00:00:49.956 --> 00:00:52.580
and Unit 6 says what it
means for this module.
